;
; TEXTEDIT on a linear dimension ([0.8.1-RT11], work #939; card PT11, point 2; ADR 0054,
; point 6). The value is the replaced text, with <> for the measurement, and <> when the
; replaced text is empty (card PT11, point 1: "value ... <> se è vuoto"): the prompt is
; "Enter new text <<>>:". The text "<> mm" shows "30 mm" and keeps the measurement
; dynamic; a second TEXTEDIT proposes "<> mm" and writes "Quota". Each modification is
; a Textedit step: U undoes the second one, REDO repeats it.
; Dimension as dimlinear/mtext (ISO-25, text above the line, 1.875 over it, not moved
; by its content, which fits between the extension lines): origins 0,0 and 30,0, line
; at y = 10, so line-point 30,10 and text-point 15,11.875; measurement 30. The
; dimension line is chosen with the typed point 5,10, away from the text.
; The location prompt of DIMLINEAR gains Mtext with PT3 (#930), hence the comment.
DIMLINEAR
0,0
30,0
; cambia con #930
15,10
TEXTEDIT
5,10
<> mm

!report
TEXTEDIT
5,10
Quota

!report
U
!report
REDO
